  faqs: [
    { question: "How does someone in Ongole go about finding an IB tutor?", answer: "Send over the programme, subject and level, and say plainly what is not working at the moment. Prakasam district has no IB school of its own, so the hunt goes national, we settle on a lesson time around your evenings, and a free trial class happens before you owe anything. If that first tutor does not click, we look again." },
    { question: "Is there someone who teaches Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE specifically?", answer: "Yes, either board, matched to whichever code and tier your child's school actually runs, Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel. Lessons happen over video, not in your home. Mathematics 0580 Extended and Chemistry 0620 are frequent requests, and every session works off that board's real past papers." },
    { question: "Do tutors come to the house here in Ongole?", answer: "No, that does not happen in Ongole. House visits are limited to Gurugram and pockets of Delhi NCR. What you actually get is a live, one-to-one video class with a shared screen doing the work a physical notebook otherwise would, which is proper tuition, just not delivered at your gate." },
    { question: "What kind of fee should we budget for?", answer: "Scarcity drives the number far more than difficulty does. IB Diploma HL costs more than Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE Core because so few tutors nationally have recently taught HL content. Your figure is fixed before the trial, travel adds nothing since it is all online, and stopping whenever you like is never a problem." },
    { question: "Does any school in Ongole run the IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None do. Not one school across Prakasam district, Ongole, Markapur, Addanki or Chimakurthy included, carries IB, Cambridge or Edexcel authorisation. The AP State Board and CBSE handle nearly all local education, which pushes any family after an international curriculum toward Vijayawada or beyond." },
    { question: "My daughter is at Bloomingdale International School in Vijayawada. Can you support her during breaks?", answer: "Absolutely, we hear this from Ongole regularly given how close Vijayawada actually is. We match to the exact IB subject and level her school teaches, scheduling around her holidays or, where the school permits it, evening slots while term is running." },
    { question: "Do you offer a trial before any payment?", answer: "Every match opens that way. Your child tackles a genuine topic from their real syllabus, at no cost, with zero pressure to continue afterward. A month-one plan only gets sent once you have decided the tutor is worth keeping." },
    { question: "Will the tutor draft or fix an Internal Assessment for my child?", answer: "No, that crosses a line we do not cross. Support means settling on a workable question, breaking down what each criterion rewards, and giving straight feedback on drafts. Actually writing it, or rewriting it, breaks IB rules outright." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects are available for a student based in Ongole?", answer: "Support spans both Maths courses (Analysis and Approaches, and Applications and Interpretation), the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, along with Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay. The tutor is picked for the specific HL or SL level." },
    { question: "Can you help with MYP or PYP too, or is this only for Diploma students?", answer: "We cover all of it. A younger child enrolled at an international school elsewhere gets support with MYP's criteria-based grading and the Personal Project, or with PYP reading, number work and inquiry research, depending on their stage." },
    { question: "Does online tutoring work as well as sitting in a classroom with a teacher?", answer: "Given that nobody near Ongole specialises in these subjects to begin with, tutoring delivered online is usually the stronger option, not a compromise. A shared screen lets a tutor mark work live or sketch a diagram exactly as needed, while giving you access to specialists across India instead of nobody at all locally." },
    { question: "How thoroughly are these tutors actually screened?", answer: "Nobody gets introduced to a family before we confirm qualifications, recent teaching experience with that precise subject and level, and their approach to Internal Assessment support. Given Ongole's thin local pool, recent syllabus experience weighs more with us than a generic CV, and the trial class lets you verify the rest yourself." },
    { question: "What age or class should tutoring start at?", answer: "Ideally right when the course opens, Class 11 for the Diploma or Grade 9 for IGCSE, so gaps get fixed before internal exams and predicted grades stack up together. A later start still helps, with sessions focused tightly on the highest-value topics." },
    { question: "How rough is switching from the AP State Board or CBSE into IGCSE?", answer: "It is a frequent question among Ongole families considering a different school. Content rarely trips students up; question style does. Words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need a different kind of answer than a State Board or CBSE paper expects, so it pays to start that adjustment a term early." },
    { question: "Are weekend or evening sessions an option?", answer: "Yes, and that is when most Ongole families schedule, weekday evenings after school plus weekend mornings. We shift sessions earlier in the evening during peak summer heat, and build in flexibility for the October-to-December cyclone season when a storm warning can force a last-minute reschedule." },
    { question: "What if things are not working out with the assigned tutor?", answer: "Just say so and we swap them out. Check-ins happen every few weeks specifically to catch problems before they fester, and since there is no long contract binding you, changing tutors costs nothing." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram tied to any school in Ongole or Vijayawada, or to the exam boards themselves?", answer: "Not at all. We run independently of every school mentioned on this page and of the IB, Cambridge and Edexcel, and tutors work strictly to whatever syllabus and calendar a student's actual school has set." },
  ],

